WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.120
Hi everyone,

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.640
You are on English Online,&nbsp;
the Business English series.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.080
Today we are following on with our second tip for&nbsp;
building resilience, so let’s jump straight in.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:16.800
Tip number two is about using different writing&nbsp;
techniques to gain a more objective perspective.&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.160
This might sound like a&nbsp;
strange one, but bear with me.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:27.040
I was never someone who was into keeping diaries&nbsp;
or writing journals or anything like that, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:33.360
even I have clearly seen some benefits of applying&nbsp;
writing techniques into my day-to-day life.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.320
As humans, we tend to have this ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:42.640
to over-exaggerate everything, and make&nbsp;
everything seem way worse than it actually is.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.880
This is true for both positive&nbsp;
and negative situations.&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:52.320
When encountering a negative situation, by taking&nbsp;
a couple of minutes to write down what happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:01:00.480
and I mean what actually happened, some facts and&nbsp;
some bullet points, it allows us to remove our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:08.080
emotions that may have clouded our judgement and&nbsp;
it allows us to gain a more objective perspective.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.520
This morning’s meeting was an&nbsp;
absolute mess. We were late&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.400
starting. The presentation really didn’t&nbsp;
go down well. Felt like an absolute idiot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:27.120
how embarrassing. I think that we need to make&nbsp;
lots of improvements. He seemed super unimpressed.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:32.800
That meeting did not go well, okay,&nbsp;
so. Meeting was at 10am. We were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:40.960
meeting to discuss the contract. Negative&nbsp;
aspects, negative aspects and positives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:47.360
well, I felt like I didn’t speak very well. 
 
Taking a minute to jot down ten bullet points&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:53.040
will take less than 10 minutes, so next time&nbsp;
you encounter a difficult situation, try this:

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.520
Write down four facts and&nbsp;
figures from the situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:03.680
three positives and three negative outcomes&nbsp;
and make sure that you are objective.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.400
We can also look at our reaction and&nbsp;
if there’s anything that we would’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:13.600
changed or done differently. This helps&nbsp;
us to be more prepared for the next time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:19.680
that we encounter a similar situation and&nbsp;
teaches us to take things less personally.
 
 &nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:25.360
Alternatively, you may be somebody who&nbsp;
writes down or jots down any of the little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.080
things that is annoying them, frustrating&nbsp;
them or getting them down. By doing this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.760
you can also practise the art of letting go by&nbsp;
burning the sheet of paper with all of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:42.640
annoyances or ripping it up, blowing it away and&nbsp;
letting go of all of your stress and worries.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:49.200
If you can think of any other writing techniques&nbsp;
that you have benefitted from to help build&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:03:04.240
resilience and lower your stress level then&nbsp;
please share them in the comments below.

